      "kind": "waiver",
      "edge_id": {
        "entry_key": "ConventionResolveService",
        "anchor_id": {
          "file_path": "track/items/consumer-convention-ownership-and-harness-decoupling-2026-07-25/spec.json",
          "element_id": "AC-06"
        }
      },
      "reason": "ConventionResolveService declares one method: resolve(&self, query: ResolveConventionsQuery) -> Result<ConventionResolution, ConventionResolveError>. AC-06 promises three things of the command: that the paths it returns are exactly those whose required_for contains the named capability id under whole-value equality, that those paths arrive without duplicates and in stable order, and that resolving creates, updates, deletes and indexes nothing. This declaration establishes none of the three. The signature relates nothing in the query to the value returned, so an implementor may answer any resolution for any capability id; a stand-in bound here can only hand back what the test arranged for it, and the test would exhibit that arrangement rather than the matching AC-06 promises. Deduplication and stable order are guarantees of ConventionResolution, established where that value is constructed from its matches; this declaration selects that type as its success value and therefore inherits those guarantees rather than establishing them, so a test bound here would be verifying the returned type's constructor under this entry's name. Read-only-ness does not follow from the signature either: &self denies the caller an exclusive borrow, which says nothing about what an implementation may do to the filesystem while answering, and returning a value is not a statement that nothing was written to produce it. What this declaration does establish is narrower than any of the three and is not what AC-06 promises: that a caller receives exactly one resolution value, through exactly one operation, or else a declared failure. AC-06's three promises are verified where they are produced -- whole-value matching where a requirement compares an identifier and the selection applies that comparison, deduplication and ordering where the resolution value is constructed, and the read at the adapter that performs it."
    },
